      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- TIP_DETAIL\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- department name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- courses: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- course material: TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\n\n## Join Keys\n- TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"Chemistry\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry'\"\n- \"Course 5\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, give the department name and find the average and standard deviation of the number of enrolled students in courses that have at least one associated course material, but only for the Chemistry department.\n```sql\nSELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, AVG(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrolled_students, STDDEV(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS stddev_enrolled_students FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON tso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID WHERE tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry' AND td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY IS NOT NULL GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each department, provide the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in courses that have at least one associated course material, and for each department also include a grand total row for all departments in the format of (null, total average, total stddev). Do not return any rounded answers."
