      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"id\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) subject offered table: one row per subject offered in a term within the textbook program scope, with subject identity, offering department/school, responsible faculty, enrollment count, and a flag indicating whether the subject has no course material. Parent of TIP_DETAIL via TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\", \"columns\": {\"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the TIP subject offered record; joins to TIP_DETAIL.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code in YYYYTT format; joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, \"IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject has no course material; 'N' means the subject has course materials\"}, \"MASTER_COURSE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Course number of the master subject\"}, \"MASTER_COURSE_NUMBER_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the master course number\"}, \"MASTER_COURSE_NUMBER_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Description of the master course number\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Master subject identifier for clustered subjects\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the master subject identifier\"}, \"COURSE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Course number of the subject\"}, \"COURSE_NUMBER_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the course number\"}, \"COURSE_NUMBER_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Course number description\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier, e.g. '5.01'; joins to TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the subject identifier\"}, \"SUBJECT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Subject title\"}, \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department code; joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE and STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"OFFER_DEPT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department name, e.g. 'Chemistry', 'Mathematics'\"}, \"OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Offering school name\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the faculty member responsible for the subject\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"MIT ID of the responsible faculty member\"}, \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of students enrolled in the subject; used for enrollment-based rankings and window statistics\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per subject per term in the textbook program\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) detail table linking subjects offered in a term to their course textbook materials: material key, material status (e.g. 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options), ISBN, and record count. Used to determine whether subjects have required textbooks and to count course materials per status.\", \"columns\": {\"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Foreign key to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\"}, \"TIP_MATERIAL_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Foreign key to TIP_MATERIAL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY identifying the specific textbook material\"}, \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Material status key; joins to TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY for decoding. Value domain includes 'RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'RC' = Recommended, 'PC' = Val-u option, 'BR' = Bookstore recommends, 'CL' = Go to class first, 'NM' = Course has no materials, 'U' = Unknown, and 'NL'/'NS'/'NB'/blank keys with no description. Distinct from LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, which belongs to the library reserve domain.\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code in YYYYTT format; joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier, e.g. '18.01'; joins to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID, SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\"}, \"ISBN\": {\"desc\": \"ISBN of the textbook material associated with the subject offering\"}, \"RECORD_COUNT\": {\"desc\": \"Number of material records for this subject/material combination; used in material-count statistics\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per subject-material-status combination per term\", \"entity\": {\"columns\": {\"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Material status key; joins to TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY for decoding. Value domain includes 'RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'RC' = Recommended, 'PC' = Val-u option, 'BR' = Bookstore recommends, 'CL' = Go to class first, 'NM' = Course has no materials, 'U' = Unknown, and 'NL'/'NS'/'NB' = None variants. Distinct from LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, which belongs to the library reserve domain.\"}}}, \"reason\": \"Data verification of TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS shows 12 status values beyond the previously documented 'RQ'/'EO'; enriching the description supports material-status grouping questions such as case dw_2989 (per material status and publisher statistics).\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS\", \"name\": \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS\", \"desc\": \"TIP material status lookup table decoding material status keys/codes used in TIP_DETAIL. Holds 12 status rows where key and code are identical: 'RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'RC' = Recommended, 'PC' = Val-u option, 'BR' = Bookstore recommends, 'CL' = Go to class first, 'NM' = Course has no materials, 'U' = Unknown, and four keys ('NL', 'NS', 'NB', and a blank/space key) that share a NULL description.\", \"columns\": {\"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the material status; joins to TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\"}, \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Material status code, identical in value to TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY: 'RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'RC' = Recommended, 'PC' = Val-u option, 'BR' = Bookstore recommends, 'CL' = Go to class first, 'NM' = Course has no materials, 'U' = Unknown, plus NULL-description keys 'NL', 'NS', 'NB' and a blank key.\"}, \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS\": {\"desc\": \"Material status description text. NULL for four of the twelve keys ('NL', 'NS', 'NB', blank), so grouping by this column merges those keys into one NULL group and yields fewer distinct statuses than grouping by key.\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per material status\"}, {\"columns\": [\"SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Measure meaning\", \"detail\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is the headcount of students enrolled (present in SUBJECT_OFFERED at section grain, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY at subject grain, and in TIP/LIBRARY program snapshots); SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER is the official subject enrollment number recorded by the registrar (SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY)\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Grain\", \"detail\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is per section; SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is per subject per term; SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER is the final subject-level enrollment with weekly/credit/listener breakdowns available in sibling columns\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Program scope\", \"detail\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED and LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED enrollment values are snapshots within the textbook-program and library-reserve scopes respectively and may not cover all subjects\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions about official subject enrollment (e.g. 'subject enrollment number greater than 10')\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER.\", \"Questions about number of enrolled students per subject offering or per department totals\": \"Use NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS from SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject grain) or SUBJECT_OFFERED (section grain, needs aggregation).\", \"Questions about enrollment of subjects within the textbook program or library reserve scope\": \"Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS or LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS respectively.\", \"Questions needing enrollment timing (first week, fifth week) or credit vs listener splits\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY's SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_FIRST_WEEK / FIFTH_WEEK and *_CREDIT / *_LISTEN columns.\"}, \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\", \"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"name\": \"Enrollment Measures\"}, {\"columns\": [\"TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\", \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\", \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\", \"LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Program\", \"detail\": \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY belongs to the textbook program (decoded by TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS); LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY belongs to library reserve processing (decoded by LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS). The two key domains are independent and must not be joined to each other.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Value domains\", \"detail\": \"TIP statuses: 'RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'RC' = Recommended, 'PC' = Val-u option, 'BR' = Bookstore recommends, 'CL' = Go to class first, 'NM' = Course has no materials, 'U' = Unknown, plus 'NL'/'NS'/'NB'/blank keys with NULL descriptions. Library statuses: 'U' = Unknown, 'R' = NULL description, 'N' = Non-Required Course Material, 'O' = Reserve only, 'X' = No Required Textbook, 'Y' = Required Course Material. Both domains contain 'U' but it means 'Unknown' in each program independently.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Usage pattern\", \"detail\": \"Fact-side filtering uses the key columns on TIP_DETAIL / LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL directly; the lookup tables provide human-readable status text when needed. Grouping by the description column instead of the key merges statuses with NULL or identical descriptions.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Cross-domain equality risk\", \"detail\": \"Some warehouse analyses equate TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY with LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY to attach per-status statistics across the two programs. Because the value domains are independent, such an equality only matches on coincidental code overlap (e.g. 'U') and carries semantic risk; results should be interpreted as code-level matching, not as a true business relationship between textbook status and library reserve status.\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions about required or optional textbooks\": \"Filter TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY IN ('RQ','EO'); 'RQ' for required only.\", \"Questions about library reserve material status\": \"Filter/group LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY (e.g. 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material); decode text via LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS.\", \"Questions needing status description text rather than codes\": \"Join TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS or LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS on the respective key; note that description columns contain NULLs for some keys.\", \"Matching reserve materials to textbook materials\": \"Match via SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE (or TIP_MATERIAL_KEY paths) between TIP_DETAIL and LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL, never by equating the two status key columns.\", \"Questions about required textbooks or textbook material statuses\": \"Filter/group TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY (e.g. 'RQ' for Required); decode text via TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS.\"}, \"desc\": \"Material status key columns of the textbook program (TIP) and library reserve program. Both are coded status references decoded by their own lookup tables (key value equals code value), with independent value domains: TIP statuses ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, 'RC' Recommended, 'PC' Val-u option, 'BR' Bookstore recommends, 'CL' Go to class first, 'NM' Course has no materials, 'U' Unknown, plus NULL-description keys) vs library reserve statuses ('U' Unknown, 'R' null description, 'N' Non-Required Course Material, 'O' Reserve only, 'X' No Required Textbook, 'Y' Required Course Material).\", \"id\": \"column_concept_material_status_key\", \"name\": \"Material Status Key\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"name\": \"Department Name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\", \"columns\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT\", \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Naming convention\", \"detail\": \"DEPARTMENT_NAME is used by catalog/summary tables (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY), department/course lookup tables, and the student directory (MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY); OFFER_DEPT_NAME is used by offering/program tables (SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED) and denotes the department that actually offers the subject; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR uses the plain column name DEPARTMENT for the course's academic department; SE_PERSON uses ORGANIZATION for the person's organizational unit\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Value format\", \"detail\": \"Catalog, summary, offering, student-directory, and lookup tables store plain department names (e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry', 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'); LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT stores a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics', '06 - Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), with some unprefixed values (e.g. 'Architecture'), so it is not directly comparable to plain-name columns without stripping the prefix\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Academic vs HR/organization value domain\", \"detail\": \"Catalog, summary, offering, library, student-directory, and lookup tables share the academic department domain; EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME is the HR organizational unit name and has a different domain (e.g. 'Lincoln Laboratory', 'Department of Physics'), where some values coincide with academic names but many do not, and some carry a 'Department of ...' prefix; SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION holds organizational unit names that may use different naming variants than the academic domain for the same unit (e.g. 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science' vs the academic 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), so equality filters across the two conventions must use each table's own variant\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion code column\", \"detail\": \"Catalog/summary tables carry DEPARTMENT_CODE joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; offering/program tables carry OFFER_DEPT_CODE joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE or STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY carries DEPARTMENT (the academic department code) joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, which is the reliable join key instead of the name; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR has no department code column, only the prefixed name text; EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY carries DEPARTMENT_NUMBER (HR department number) and SE_PERSON carries no department code, neither joining to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Filtering subjects by department in catalog or summary analysis\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME or SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME.\", \"Filtering by department in section-level, textbook-program, or library analysis\": \"Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Joining fact tables to department dimension attributes (school, full name, degree-granting)\": \"Prefer code joins: DEPARTMENT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; name equality joins are used when codes are unavailable.\", \"Matching departments across a DEPARTMENT_NAME table and an OFFER_DEPT_NAME table\": \"The values are directly comparable (same academic name domain), e.g. joining SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME.\", \"Filtering employees by their HR organizational unit (e.g. names containing 'Department', or HR units like 'Political Science')\": \"Use EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME; do not join it to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, and pair it with DEPARTMENT_NUMBER for HR grouping.\", \"Filtering by department in section-level, textbook-program, or library subject analysis\": \"Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Filtering library reserve course instructors by academic department or library unit\": \"Use LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT with the prefixed value format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); do not compare it directly to plain department-name columns.\", \"Filtering students by their academic department\": \"Use MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT (code) joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE for reliable matching, or MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME for direct name filters; the name shares the academic domain with SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME.\", \"Filtering a person master (SE_PERSON) record by organizational unit such as an academic department\": \"Use SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION with its own naming variant (e.g. 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science'); do not equate it directly to MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME or SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, which use the academic variant (e.g. 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci').\"}}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"name\": \"Course Material and Library Reserve Domain\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\", \"tables\": [\"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"TIP_MATERIAL\", \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\", \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG\", \"LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS\", \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Business process\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / TIP_DETAIL / TIP_MATERIAL / TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS\": \"Textbook program: subjects tracked for textbook adoption, material rows with status and ISBN, material bibliographic details, status decoding\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL / LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG / LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS / LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR\": \"Library reserve: subjects in reserve processing, reserve material detail rows, catalog item bibliographic records, status decoding, instructor assignments\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Status semantics\", \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\": \"12 statuses decoded by TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS: 'RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'RC' = Recommended, 'PC' = Val-u option, 'BR' = Bookstore recommends, 'CL' = Go to class first, 'NM' = Course has no materials, 'U' = Unknown, plus NULL-description keys 'NL'/'NS'/'NB'/blank\", \"LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\": \"6 statuses decoded by LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS: 'U' = Unknown, 'R' = NULL description, 'N' = Non-Required Course Material, 'O' = Reserve only, 'X' = No Required Textbook, 'Y' = Required Course Material\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Count measures\", \"TIP_DETAIL\": \"COUNT(TIP_MATERIAL_KEY) or RECORD_COUNT for material-count statistics per status/subject\", \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\": \"COUNT(LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY) for reserve catalog item counts per status/subject; LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG.RECORD_COUNTER is a catalog record counter\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Parent-child structure\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED → TIP_DETAIL\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY / SUBJECT_ID links subject rows to material rows\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED → LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL → LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY and LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY chain subjects to reserve items\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions about required/optional textbooks, ISBNs, or whether subjects have course materials\": \"Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL flag) with TIP_DETAIL (TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY 'RQ'/'EO').\", \"Questions about library reserve items, reserve counts per subject, or catalog titles/authors\": \"Use LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL joined to LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG, scoped by LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Questions about enrollment of subjects within the textbook program or library reserve scope\": \"Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS or LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS respectively; these are program-specific snapshots, not the official SUBJECT_SUMMARY enrollment.\", \"Questions about textbook prices, editions, or publishers\": \"Use TIP_MATERIAL via TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY.\", \"Questions about instructors of courses with reserve materials\": \"Use LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR via LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY.\", \"Questions about required textbooks, ISBNs, or whether subjects have course materials\": \"Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL flag) with TIP_DETAIL (TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, e.g. 'RQ' Required).\", \"Questions combining textbook material statuses with library reserve statuses\": \"Join TIP_DETAIL and LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL on SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE, decode each status via its own lookup table, and aggregate each side separately; never equate the two status key columns.\"}}], \"not_found\": []}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_568e61f33eda4c69958b6182",
      "name": "semantic_graph",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 20, \"items\": [{\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) detail table linking subjects offered in a term to their course textbook materials: material key, material status (e.g. 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options), ISBN, and record count. Used to determine whether subjects have required textbooks and to count course materials per status.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"TIP_DETAIL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Academic term dimension table describing each academic term's calendar and status attributes: term code/description, start/end dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, key registration and class dates, and term status classification (Previous/Current/Future, regular vs non-regular term). Used to filter and enrich subject offerings by term characteristics.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"name\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"SIS department dimension table: academic departments with code, name, full name, school attribution (code and name), budget code, degree-granting flag, and commencement-book names. Joins to subject offering tables via department codes.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"name\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Student-facing department lookup table with department code, name, full name, and school attribution (code and name). Similar in content to SIS_DEPARTMENT but oriented to student information systems reporting; joins to offering tables via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\", \"name\": \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Course catalog subject offering table recording catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year and term: subject identity (SUBJECT_ID = SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER), department, unit structure (lecture/lab/preparation/design/total units), grading type and rules, HGN level (Undergraduate/Graduate/High Graduate), requirement attributes (GIR, HASS, communication, writing), term offering flags (this year, fall, IAP, spring, summer), instructors, section flags, responsible faculty, and meeting time/place. Links to terms via both TERM_CODE (the offering term) and EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (the term from which catalog attributes take effect).\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Library subject offered table: subjects offered per term that appear in library reserve processing, with subject identity, course number, offering department/school, responsible faculty, and enrollment count. Parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Extended academic term dimension table covering all terms known to the warehouse (a superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS, including terms without full status tracking). Shares term calendar attributes (term code, dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, registration and class dates) but does not carry IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS, ADD_DATE or DROP_DATE columns.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\", \"name\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Term parameter reference table holding exactly three rows that identify the SIS current term, previous term, and upcoming term, each with its term code, description, start/end dates and the last day before the next term. Used to resolve relative term references ('C', 'P', 'F') to concrete term codes.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\", \"name\": \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) subject offered table: one row per subject offered in a term within the textbook program scope, with subject identity, offering department/school, responsible faculty, enrollment count, and a flag indicating whether the subject has no course material. Parent of TIP_DETAIL via TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) subject offered table: one row per subject offered in a term within the textbook program scope, with subject identity, offering department/school, responsible faculty, enrollment count, and a flag indicating whether the subject has no course material. Parent of TIP_DETAIL via TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"SIS subject code lookup table mapping subject codes and course numbers to their descriptions, departments, and schools. Used to resolve subject code descriptions and to link courses to departments via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\", \"name\": \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Library reserve material detail bridge table linking reserve catalog items, library subject offerings, course instructors, and material status per term. Used to count reserved materials per subject and to filter by library material status (e.g. 'U').\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Section-level subject offering fact table: one row per subject section offered in a term, with section flags (master/lecture/lab/recitation/design), cluster information, offering department and school, responsible faculty, meeting time/place, and enrollment numbers at section, subject, and cluster level. Linked to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject level) via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY/COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY and to SUBJECT_SUMMARY via SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\", \"entity_type\": \"concept\", \"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"name\": \"Subject Offering Fact Tables\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\", \"entity_type\": \"concept\", \"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"name\": \"Course Material and Library Reserve Domain\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"name\": \"Term Code\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"name\": \"Subject Identifier\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"name\": \"Department Name\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"name\": \"Enrollment Measures\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Master subject identifier columns (MASTER_SUBJECT_ID and its sortable variant MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT) replicated across the registrar offering tables, the subject summary, the textbook program, the library reserve program, and the CIS course catalog. For clustered subjects (e.g. joint or cross-listed offerings), the master subject identifier points to the leading subject of the cluster, so joining on it matches offerings that share the same master subject even when their own SUBJECT_ID differs. SUBJECT_ID/SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the subject itself, while MASTER_SUBJECT_ID/MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the cluster's master; the _SORT columns are the sortable forms of the same values used for cross-table joins.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_master_subject_id\", \"name\": \"Master Subject Identifier\"}]}"
