led with `1045 Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`; database unreachable, noted explicitly.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Recommended tables/columns:**\n- `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` (alias tso): `OFFER_DEPT_NAME` (grouping/output), `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (measure), `SUBJECT_ID` (join key).\n- `TIP_DETAIL` (alias td): `SUBJECT_ID` (join key), `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY` (material-existence filter `IS NOT NULL`).\n\n**6b. Recommended SQL approach:** inner join tso↔td on SUBJECT_ID (exactly as the gold decomposition), filter `td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY IS NOT NULL`, no department filter (question covers all departments — the 'Chemistry' domain-knowledge line belongs to the sub-decomposition variant only), `GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME WITH ROLLUP` so MySQL emits per-department rows plus the super-aggregate `(NULL, overall AVG, overall STDDEV)` row. Use bare `STDDEV()` per the tip. No rounding.\n\n**6c. Three-perspective reasons:**\n- **Data**: both required columns physically exist (retrieved column defs); SUBJECT_ID is the documented cross-table join key on both tables; ROLLUP produces exactly the `(null, total avg, total stddev)` shape. Caveat: SUBJECT_ID-only join fans out per material/term row — accepted because the gold precedent computes AVG/STDDEV over the joined population the same way.\n- **Semantic-network**: concept_course_material_programs decision guide routes \"whether subjects have course materials\" to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED + TIP_DETAIL; enrollment_measures decision guide routes textbook-program enrollment to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS; department_name concept confirms OFFER_DEPT_NAME as the offering-table convention; graph shows the TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED↔TIP_DETAIL join edge.\n- **Business**: the provided gold decomposition is exactly this query restricted to Chemistry; precedents dw_1350/dw_1288/dw_3911 establish the `(null, …)` grand-total row format; 15+ metrics establish the bare-STDDEV, no-rounding convention.\n\n**6d. Alternatives